$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\Large \frac\pi2}\dfrac{-\cos(x)}{\left(x-\dfrac\pi2\right)}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\Large  \frac\pi2}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}[-\cos(x)]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[x-\dfrac\pi2\right]}\qquad\gray{\text{L’Hôpital’s rule}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\Large  \frac\pi2}\dfrac{\sin(x)}{1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\sin\left(\dfrac\pi2\right)}{1}\qquad\gray{\text{Substitution}}
\\\\
&=1
\end{align}$

Note that we were only able to use L’Hôpital’s rule because the limit $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\Large  \frac\pi2}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}[-\cos(x)]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[x-\dfrac\pi2\right]}$ actually exists.
